From ca7aa3ae2009ade951fee7a593fd884cc4442ba3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nyasha <nmushambi@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:06:49 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 02/29] Pulse the panel reset and log the panel's DCS state

- Assert then release the panel reset line; driving it high alone leaves the
  panel in whatever state survived the previous SoC reboot
- Read GET_POWER_MODE, GET_PIXEL_FORMAT and GET_ADDRESS_MODE after init to
  tell a dummy read from a panel that is ignoring commands
- Both still return 0x00 and some writes time out (-110), so the panel is
  not reaching a usable display-on state yet

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code with DeepSeek Flash v4.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lpm089a128a.c | 13 ++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lpm089a128a.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lpm089a128a.c
index 59fd547a8..670006359 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lpm089a128a.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-jdi-lpm089a128a.c
@@ -196,10 +196,17 @@ static int jdi_panel_prepare(struct drm_panel *panel)
 	usleep_range(JDI_POWER_UP_DELAY_MS * 1000,
 		     JDI_POWER_UP_DELAY_MS * 1000 + 500);
 
-	/* Reset is active high as the device tree declares it. */
+	/*
+	 * Reset is active high as the device tree declares it, but the panel
+	 * must actually be pulsed: driving it high without first asserting it
+	 * leaves the panel in whatever state survived the previous SoC reboot.
+	 * That state is not reliably usable -- after a DSI reset without a
+	 * panel reset, every DCS command times out with -110.
+	 */
+	gpiod_set_value(jdi->reset_gpio, 0);
+	usleep_range(10000, 12000);
 	gpiod_set_value(jdi->reset_gpio, 1);
-	usleep_range(JDI_POWER_UP_DELAY_MS * 1000,
-		     JDI_POWER_UP_DELAY_MS * 1000 + 500);
+	usleep_range(120000, 121000);
 
 	/*
 	 * No column/page address setup: the downstream init table has neither
-- 
